# Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env.local
```

## Variables

| Variable | Description | Required |
|----------|-------------|----------|
| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | API key for Gemini AI calls | Yes |
| `APP_URL` | URL where the app is hosted | Yes |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_AMAZON_TRACKING_ID` | Amazon Associates tracking ID for affiliate links | Yes (for shop) |

## Example

```env
GEMINI_API_KEY="your-gemini-api-key"
APP_URL="https://your-app-url.com"
NEXT_PUBLIC_AMAZON_TRACKING_ID="your-amazon-associates-id"
```

## Security

- `.env` files are **gitignored** and never committed
- Only variables prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` are exposed to the browser
- Store your secret keys (like `GEMINI_API_KEY`) server-side only